---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Scene from "../components/scene/Scene.astro";
import Signature from "../components/Signature.astro";
import { ORG_URL } from "../lib/seo";
---

<Base
  title="About these guides"
  description="Who writes the buymyvisa travel guides, how we check visa and entry rules, and where the photos come from."
>
  <Scene name="home" max="56vh">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h1>About these guides</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Scene>
  <div class="narrow prose">
    <p>
      <a href={ORG_URL}>buymyvisa</a> files visas and arrival cards for travel companies and their travellers. We
      spend our days inside government visa forms, so we write down what we learn: what each country asks of an Indian
      passport, what a trip really costs, and how to see the best of it in a week or so.
    </p>
    <h2>How we check facts</h2>
    <p>
      Visa and entry rules are checked against each country's official site before a guide is published, and every
      guide shows the date of that check. Prices are per person in Indian rupees for a mid-range trip in the season we
      recommend, excluding shopping. Exchange rates move, so treat them as a guide, not a quote.
    </p>
    <h2>Photos and illustrations</h2>
    <p>
      Photos are from <a href="https://unsplash.com/?utm_source=buymyvisa&utm_medium=referral">Unsplash</a>, credited
      under each one. The landscapes at the top of each page are drawn for this site, and the sky follows your clock:
      dawn, day, dusk or night.
    </p>
    <p>Spotted something out of date? Write to <a href="mailto:visa@buymyvisa.com">visa@buymyvisa.com</a>.</p>
    <Signature />
  </div>
</Base>
